A box holds three counters: one green one labelled $G$ and two yellow ones labelled $Y_{1}$ and $Y_{2}$. One counter is drawn and kept, then a second counter is drawn. Every counter is equally likely to be picked at each draw, so the six paths of the tree are equally likely. What is the probability that the two counters are different colours, as a fraction in simplest form?
